name 'thinking-critically-about-ai-postassessment-q1_2026-pilot_2026'

question 'A school uses an AI system to predict which students are likely to struggle academically and flags them for extra support. A teacher notices the system flags students from lower-income neighborhoods at much higher rates. What is the most likely explanation?'

wrong 'The AI system is working correctly because income is the best predictor of academic struggle.'
wrong 'The AI system has a glitch that can be fixed by restarting it.'
right 'The AI was likely trained on historical data that reflected existing inequalities, so it learned and is now reproducing those biases.'
wrong 'The AI system is intentionally discriminating against students from lower-income neighborhoods.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lessons 2, 6
MARKDOWN
